  "comparison": "The indicative 2018 DSM median roof-surface height (~60 ft AGL) is close to the inherited model L5 slab datum (~58.8 ft). It makes a roof-level slab interpretation plausible but cannot establish that L5 is a roof slab, an occupied floor, or exactly registered in vertical datum. The GIS extraction attribute of 48 ft remains conflicting and its semantics are not surveyed height.",
  "limitations": [
    "5 ft DSM cell spacing and approximate footprint conversion limit local feature attribution.",
    "The DSM median combines roof planes, lower surfaces, edges and rooftop objects; it does not measure the parapet, penthouse, or a specific facade point.",
    "The bare-earth surface is modeled/interpolated under the building; the 21 samples are service queries inside the footprint, not surveyed building footings.",
    "Absolute accuracy specifications for QL2 are statewide metrics, not a Knoy-specific accuracy assessment.",
    "The 2018 surface snapshot does not prove 2026 roof configuration.",
    "This assessment does not register the PV mesh to the 2023 orthophoto; withdrawn cyan PV bounds remain do-not-use."
